=== Stamps vs no-stamps legibility probe (frozen catmus CER, spec §6.5.30) 20260823 ===
100 medical texts (AnatMondG), rendered WITH stamps (medical_1font) and NO stamps (matched),
GT = original_text (base letters). Same 100 lines both ways.

                 raw      +gentle   +harsh
  WITH stamps    0.1511   0.1517    0.2006
  NO stamps      0.0596   0.0569    0.1167

FINDING: stamps add a large RAW legibility penalty (0.151 vs 0.060, 2.5x) BEFORE augmentation —
frozen catmus can't map the composited scribal glyphs (tironian, abbrev, capitals, ligatures)
to the clean base-letter GT (the "stamp bleed" of §6.5.24). Gentle aug barely changes either;
harsh adds ~0.05-0.06. So the STAMPS are a bigger frozen-reader legibility hit than gentle aug.
Caveat: measures a model that never trained on the stamps; a trained model learns the mappings.
Reinforces why the leader's no-stamps renders read clean (~0.06).
